<title>SWITZERLAND: Memphis is top Feb 97 world cargo airport - ACI.</title>
<headline>Memphis is top Feb 97 world cargo airport - ACI.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Memphis, headquarters of U.S. express freight carrier, Federal Express, was the world's busiest cargo airport in February 1997, said Geneva-based Airports Council International (ACI) in a survey of 486 airports worldwide.</p>
<p>The world's 20 busiest cargo airports in February 1997, with the volume they handled (in tonnes and the percentage change over February 1996, were as follows:</p>
<p>    1  (1)   Memphis	   163,965 tonnes     up   16.0 pct</p>
<p>    2  (3)   Los Angeles     139,224		up    7.6</p>
<p>    3  (2)   Miami	     137,049		down  2.1</p>
<p>    4  (4)   Tokyo-Narita    126,956		up    1.4</p>
<p>    5  (5)   New York/JFK    119,953		down  2.7</p>
<p>    6  (6)   Frankfurt	 115,144		down  1.6</p>
<p>    7  (10)  Seoul	     112,362		up   19.3</p>
<p>    8  (8)   Hong Kong	 104,200		up    6.3</p>
<p>    9  (7)   Louisville	103,943		down  5.5</p>
<p>    10 (9)   Chicago	    95,152		down  2.3</p>
<p>    11 (13)  Singapore	  92,537		up    7.5</p>
<p>    12 (12)  London Heathrow  91,484		up    3.2</p>
<p>    13 (11)  Amsterdam	  90,385		up    0.2</p>
<p>    14 (16)  Anchorage	  81,293		up   16.2</p>
<p>    15 (15)  Paris CDG	  78,267		up    4.3</p>
<p>    16 (14)  New York Newark  76,803		up    2.4</p>
<p>    17 (17)  Atlanta	    63,242		up    0.2</p>
<p>    18 (18)  Dallas Ft Worth  62,090		up    5.3</p>
<p>    19 (19)  Dayton	     61,183		up    4.5</p>
<p>    20 (20)  Bangkok	    55,140		up    5.7</p>
<p>* includes freight and mail in transit as well as loaded + unloaded - Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
